diff --git a/DOCS/edl-mpv.rst b/DOCS/edl-mpv.rst
index aeec4b7b..3142ca4e 100644
--- a/DOCS/edl-mpv.rst
+++ b/DOCS/edl-mpv.rst
@@ -341,6 +341,23 @@ Example::
 
 Plays chapter 3 and ends with the start of chapter 7 (4 chapters later).
 
+WWPlayer isolated segment-preroll extension
+==========================================
+
+The P1 candidate accepts ``!wwplayer_preroll,version=1`` and a ``preroll``
+parameter on each segment. The mandatory header is rejected by unextended
+runtimes, preventing silent consumption of unsupported decode windows.
+
+``preroll`` is a finite, non-negative number of seconds. For a clipped
+timeline, a segment switch or seek reads this window before its source target,
+Source seek owns beginning-of-file selection; a leading RAP DTS can precede
+the reported presentation start. The authored segment start, end, duration,
+and packet presentation clipping remain unchanged. It is not a playback delay
+or a second seek. DASH and ``no_clip`` do not support this parameter.
+
+This is a WWPlayer segment-preroll extension, not upstream EDL syntax.
+Omitting ``preroll`` preserves the existing behavior.
+
